@startuml
!include style.puml

title Connection state machine, top level

state Recovering <<pending>>
state Failed <<fault>>
state Unpaired <<fault>>

[*] --> Idle
Idle --> Active : StartRequested

state Active {
  state Linking : refined in the\nnext diagram
  state Ready <<ready>>
  state Suspended <<blocked>>

  [*] --> Linking
  Linking        --> Authenticating : Subscribed
  Authenticating --> Reconciling    : AuthSucceeded
  Reconciling    --> Ready          : ReconcileDone\n[nothing unresolved]
  Reconciling    --> Suspended      : ReconcileDone\n[unresolved remain]\nor T_RESOLVE expired
  Suspended      --> Reconciling    : UserVerifiedAtPump
}

Active --> Recovering : Disconnected / Timeout / GattFailure,\nfrom any substate
Active --> Idle       : StopRequested / ScanTimeout

Authenticating --> Unpaired : AuthFailed\n[bond or key invalid]

Recovering --> Active : backoff elapsed\n[attempts < max]
Recovering --> Failed : attempts exhausted
Failed     --> Active : StartRequested

Unpaired --> [*]

note right of Reconciling
  Reconciling sits between Authenticating
  and Ready, so "no dosing on a session
  with unresolved history" holds by
  reachability, not by convention.
end note

@enduml
